[2026-01-30T08:50:11.326Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nAnalysis:\nLet me analyze this conversation chronologically to capture all technical details.\n\nThe conversation is a continuation from a previous session where multiple requirement files were being executed. The summary at the beginning indicates work on various UI/performance improvements for a research report viewing application.\n\nStarting from where the context picks up:\n\n1. **idea-af741c95-add-page-transition-animation** (completed at start):\n   - Added AnimatePresence with directional transitions for view switching in ReportView.tsx\n   - Created TAB_ORDER constant, prevTabRef, direction state\n   - handleTabChange function calculates direction based on tab index\n   - motion.div wrapper with directional x animations\n\n2. **idea-b575c9a5-lazy-load-svg-icons-to-reduce**:\n   - Created lazy loading system for SVG icons in Icons.tsx\n   - Categorized icons by usage frequency (frequently used stay sync, less used are lazy)\n   - Created withLazyWrapper HOC with Suspense fallback\n   - TypeScript passed\n\n3. **idea-b853c6e0-add-backdrop-blur-transition-o**:\n   - Staged backdrop animation in ReportShell.tsx\n   - Phase 1: fade opacity 150ms, Phase 2: blur 200ms, Phase 3: content scales in after 350ms delay\n   - Added WebkitBackdropFilter for Safari\n\n4. **idea-ba60d4a4-debounce-searchquery-filter-to**:\n   - Created useDebouncedValue.ts hook\n   - Updated ReportView.tsx to use debounced search query (150ms)\n   - Pass debouncedSearchQuery to FindingsView and SourcesView\n\n5. **idea-bcc1c46d-add-empty-state-illustrations**:\n   - Created Illustrations.tsx with 8 SVG illustrations (SearchIllustration, FolderIllustration, etc.)\n   - Created EmptyState.tsx component with type prop\n   - Updated all views and tabs to use new EmptyState\n   - Fixed naming conflict - removed old EmptyState from Cards.tsx\n   - Fixed TypeScript error with bounceTransition type: added `as const`\n\n6. **idea-db6b8f13-create-consistent-shadow-eleva**:\n   - Added elevation system to ThemeContext (elevation1, elevation2, elevation3)\n   - Radar theme: glow-based shadows with cyan accents\n   - Swiss theme: shadow-sm, shadow-md, shadow-xl\n   - Updated Cards.tsx and ThemedCards.tsx to use elevation system\n\n7. **idea-e6711f77-add-reduced-motion-support-via**:\n   - Created useReducedMotion.ts hook using matchMedia\n   - Added reducedMotion to ThemeContext\n   - Updated AnimatedNumber, AnimatedProgressRing, PulsingDot to respect reduced motion\n\n8. **idea-ec28fa56-add-smooth-sidebar-collapse-wi**:\n   - Created useSidebarCollapsed hook with localStorage persistence\n   - Created CollapseToggle component with rotating chevron\n   - Updated RadarSidebar and SwissSidebar with motion.aside and width animations\n   - Collapsed state: w-14 (56px), Expanded: w-56 (224px) for radar, w-52 (208px) for swiss\n\n9. **idea-ef0a9619-replace-per-item-animation-del** (most recent):\n   - Replaced per-item `delay: i * 0.03` with Framer Motion staggerChildren\n   - Updated SourcesView.tsx: containerVariants, itemVariants\n   - Updated EntitiesView.tsx: listContainerVariants, listItemVariants\n   - Updated PerspectivesView.tsx: selectorContainerVariants, selectorItemVariants\n   - TypeScript passed\n\nUser messages were all simple execution commands in the format: \"Execute the requirement file: idea-[hash]-[description]\"\n\nNo errors occurred during the staggerChildren implementation. Earlier errors included:\n- PulsingDot import removed accidentally (fixed)\n- bounceTransition type error (fixed with `as const`)\n- EmptyState naming conflict (removed old from Cards.tsx)\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a series of requirement files sequentially. Each requirement file contains specific UI/UX and performance improvements that must be implemented immediately without questions. The pattern is: \"Execute the requirement file: idea-[hash]-[description]\". The user expects each requirement to be fully implemented, TypeScript checked, and completed before moving to the next.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - React.lazy() and Suspense for lazy loading icons\n   - Framer Motion animations (AnimatePresence, motion.div, layoutId, staggerChildren, variants)\n   - useMemo for memoization with stable keys\n   - prefers-reduced-motion media query support (WCAG 2.1 accessibility)\n   - Focus trap pattern for modal accessibility\n   - localStorage for persisting UI state\n   - CSS backdrop-blur with staged animation timing\n   - Debouncing for search input optimization (150ms)\n   - Elevation system for consistent shadow hierarchy\n   - Virtualization with @tanstack/react-virtual\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`src/hooks/useReducedMotion.ts`** (NEW)\n     - Detects user's prefers-reduced-motion preference for accessibility\n     ```typescript\n     export function useReducedMotion(): boolean {\n       const [reducedMotion, setReducedMotion] = useState(false);\n       useEffect(() => {\n         if (typeof window === 'undefined') return;\n         const mediaQuery = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');\n         setReducedMotion(mediaQuery.matches);\n         const handleChange = (event: MediaQueryListEvent) => {\n           setReducedMotion(event.matches);\n         };\n         mediaQuery.addEventListener('change', handleChange);\n         return () => mediaQuery.removeEventListener('change', handleChange);\n       }, []);\n       return reducedMotion;\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`src/hooks/useDebouncedValue.ts`** (NEW)\n     - Debounces values to prevent excessive re-renders\n     ```typescript\n     export function useDebouncedValue<T>(value: T, delay = 150): T {\n       const [debouncedValue, setDebouncedValue] = useState<T>(value);\n       useEffect(() => {\n         const timer = setTimeout(() => setDebouncedValue(value), delay);\n         return () => clearTimeout(timer);\n       }, [value, delay]);\n       return debouncedValue;\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`src/components/report/core/ThemeContext.tsx`**\n     - Added reducedMotion to context, elevation system to themeStyles\n     ```typescript\n     interface ThemeContextValue {\n       theme: ReportTheme;\n       reducedMotion: boolean;\n     }\n     // Added to themeStyles.radar:\n     elevation1: 'shadow-[0_1px_3px_rgba(0,0,0,0.3)]',\n     elevation2: 'shadow-[0_4px_12px_rgba(0,0,0,0.4),0_0_8px_rgba(34,211,238,0.08)]',\n     elevation3: 'shadow-[0_8px_24px_rgba(0,0,0,0.5),0_0_16px_rgba(34,211,238,0.12)]',\n     // Added to themeStyles.swiss:\n     elevation1: 'shadow-sm',\n     elevation2: 'shadow-md',\n     elevation3: 'shadow-xl',\n     ```\n\n   - **`src/components/report/shared/Illustrations.tsx`** (NEW)\n     - 8 SVG illustrations with bounce animation on mount\n     - SearchIllustration, FolderIllustration, ChainBreakIllustration, DocumentsIllustration, NetworkIllustration, LightbulbIllustration, AnalysisIllustration, UsersIllustration\n\n   - **`src/components/report/shared/EmptyState.tsx`** (NEW)\n     - Component accepting type, title, description, action props\n     - Renders appropriate illustration with theme-aware styling\n\n   - **`src/components/report/ThemedSidebar.tsx`**\n     - Added collapsible sidebar with localStorage persistence\n     ```typescript\n     const SIDEBAR_COLLAPSED_KEY = 'report-sidebar-collapsed';\n     function useSidebarCollapsed() {\n       const [collapsed, setCollapsed] = useState(false);\n       useEffect(() => {\n         const stored = localStorage.getItem(SIDEBAR_COLLAPSED_KEY);\n         if (stored !== null) setCollapsed(stored === 'true');\n       }, []);\n       const toggle = () => {\n         setCollapsed(prev => {\n           const next = !prev;\n           localStorage.setItem(SIDEBAR_COLLAPSED_KEY, String(next));\n           return next;\n         });\n       };\n       return { collapsed, toggle };\n     }\n     ```\n     - CollapseToggle component with rotating chevron animation\n     - motion.aside with width transitions (56px collapsed, 224px/208px expanded)\n\n   - **`src/components/report/views/SourcesView.tsx`** (Most recent)\n     - Replaced per-item delay with staggerChildren variants\n     ```typescript\n     const containerVariants = {\n       hidden: { opacity: 0 },\n       visible: {\n         opacity: 1,\n         transition: { staggerChildren: 0.03 },\n       },\n     };\n     const itemVariants = {\n       hidden: { opacity: 0, y: 10 },\n       visible: { opacity: 1, y: 0 },\n       exit: { opacity: 0, scale: 0.95 },\n     };\n     ```\n     - SourceCard no longer takes delay prop, uses variants instead\n\n   - **`src/components/report/views/EntitiesView.tsx`** (Most recent)\n     - Added staggerChildren for entity list\n     ```typescript\n     const listContainerVariants = {\n       hidden: { opacity: 1 },\n       visible: { opacity: 1, transition: { staggerChildren: 0.03 } },\n     };\n     const listItemVariants = {\n       hidden: { opacity: 0 },\n       visible: { opacity: 1 },\n     };\n     ```\n\n   - **`src/components/report/views/PerspectivesView.tsx`** (Most recent)\n     - Added staggerChildren for perspective selector buttons\n     ```typescript\n     const selectorContainerVariants = {\n       hidden: { opacity: 1 },\n       visible: { opacity: 1, transition: { staggerChildren: 0.05 } },\n     };\n     const selectorItemVariants = {\n       hidden: { opacity: 0, scale: 0.9 },\n       visible: { opacity: 1, scale: 1 },\n     };\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **bounceTransition type error in Illustrations.tsx**: Type `{ type: string; ... }` not assignable to Transition. Fixed by adding `as const` to the type property: `type: 'spring' as const`\n   - **EmptyState naming conflict**: Cards.tsx already exported EmptyState. Fixed by removing the old simple EmptyState from Cards.tsx\n   - **\"File has not been read yet\" errors**: Attempted edits without reading files first. Fixed by reading files before editing\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Successfully implemented staggerChildren to replace per-item delay calculations, reducing JS computation\n   - All requirement files executed successfully with TypeScript validation passing\n   - No pending issues\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"Execute the requirement file: idea-b575c9a5-lazy-load-svg-icons-to-reduce\"\n   - \"Execute the requirement file: idea-b853c6e0-add-backdrop-blur-transition-o\"\n   - \"Execute the requirement file: idea-ba60d4a4-debounce-searchquery-filter-to\"\n   - \"Execute the requirement file: idea-bcc1c46d-add-empty-state-illustrations\"\n   - \"Execute the requirement file: idea-db6b8f13-create-consistent-shadow-eleva\"\n   - \"Execute the requirement file: idea-e6711f77-add-reduced-motion-support-via\"\n   - \"Execute the requirement file: idea-ec28fa56-add-smooth-sidebar-collapse-wi\"\n   - \"Execute the requirement file: idea-ef0a9619-replace-per-item-animation-del\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - None explicitly requested. The last requirement file (idea-ef0a9619) was completed successfully.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Just completed **idea-ef0a9619-replace-per-item-animation-del** which replaced per-item animation delays with Framer Motion's staggerChildren. Updated three view files:\n   - SourcesView.tsx: containerVariants/itemVariants, removed delay prop from SourceCard\n   - EntitiesView.tsx: listContainerVariants/listItemVariants in EntityTypeColumn\n   - PerspectivesView.tsx: selectorContainerVariants/selectorItemVariants for perspective buttons\n   TypeScript check passed with no errors.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   The user may provide another requirement file to execute. The pattern has been consistent: \"Execute the requirement file: idea-[hash]-[description]\". No explicit next task is pending - awaiting user's next instruction.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\mkdol\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-mkdol-dolla-res\\a8a4f9ca-6a40-4b19-853c-2be96846861c.jsonl\nPlease continue the conversation from where we left it off without asking the user any further questions. Continue with the last task that you were asked to work on."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8a4f9ca-6a40-4b19-853c-2be96846861c","uuid":"a7a81219-ac59-41ab-8b67-ac6805af1f7e","isSynthetic":true}
